Atlas assets — licence
======================

This directory holds atlas GEOMETRY, TEXTURES and LABEL SETS. It is licensed
separately from the code in this repository, which is Apache-2.0 (see the
LICENSE at the repository root).

The separation is structural, not cosmetic. If any asset here arrives under a
share-alike licence, that obligation must be able to reach the assets and the
assets alone. `tools/check-licence-separation.mjs` enforces the boundary on
every push: no code package may depend on or import this package, and no
asset bytes may be embedded in the shipped JavaScript bundle. Assets are
served as separate files, each carrying its own licence and attribution.

Licence of the assets themselves: PENDING
-----------------------------------------

The mesh source and its licence are decision D1 on DOG-2 and are not settled.
This file is the place that decision lands, and it is the only file that has
to change when it does. Nothing downstream needs to move, because the
mechanism is licence-agnostic: commissioned work-for-hire meshes and CC-BY-SA
meshes both ship through the same separated package with the same per-asset
attribution record.

Until D1 is decided, no third-party asset may be committed to this package.
Per-asset licensing is declared in `attribution.json` and rendered into the
build as `ATTRIBUTION.md`; `attribution.json` is the authority and every entry
in it must name a licence and a source.

What is here today
------------------

Only first-party placeholder geometry written for this repository, listed in
`attribution.json` as `Apache-2.0`, owned by GStack. It exists so the build,
the performance budget and the licence separation check have something real to
operate on, and it carries no third-party obligation of any kind.
